  "termsIntroTitle": "Introduction",
  "termsIntroContent": "Welcome to Qoot - the leading platform connecting restaurants and charities to combat food waste and feed the needy. By using this app, you agree to comply with the following terms and conditions. Please read them carefully before continuing to use our services.",
  "termsUserRespTitle": "User Responsibilities",
  "termsUserRespContent": "All users pledge to provide accurate and correct information during registration. Restaurants must ensure the quality and safety of the donated food. Charities must adhere to specified pickup times and not misuse the service. It is strictly prohibited to use the platform for illegal purposes or contrary to public morals.",
  "termsPrivacyTitle": "Privacy & Data Protection",
  "termsPrivacyContent": "We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal data. Information is collected only to improve the service and facilitate the donation process. We will not share your data with third parties without your explicit consent. You have the right to access, modify, or delete your data at any time through account settings.",
  "termsDonationTitle": "Donation Guidelines",
  "termsDonationContent": "The donated food must be fit for human consumption and free from any damage or spoilage. Donors must accurately specify the type of food, quantity, and expiration date. It is preferable to donate freshly cooked or properly packaged foods. The platform is not responsible for the quality of the donated food, and the responsibility lies entirely with the donor.",
  "termsFoodSafetyTitle": "Food Safety Standards",
  "termsFoodSafetyContent": "All parties must comply with local and international food safety standards. Food must be stored at safe temperatures during storage and transport. Restaurants must follow hygiene procedures when preparing food. Charities are committed to inspecting received food and ensuring its validity before distributing to beneficiaries.",
  "termsLiabilityTitle": "Liability & Disclaimers",
  "termsLiabilityContent": "Qoot platform acts only as an intermediary between donors and beneficiaries, and bears no legal responsibility for the quality of the food or any damages resulting from its consumption. The user is fully responsible for verifying the safety of the food. We are not responsible for any loss or damage resulting from the use of the platform or inability to use it.",
  "termsIPTitle": "Intellectual Property",
  "termsIPContent": "All content in the app, including logos, images, texts, and designs, is the exclusive property of Qoot platform and protected by copyright laws. It is prohibited to copy, reproduce, or distribute any content without prior written permission. Users retain ownership of the content they publish, but grant the platform a non-exclusive license to use it.",
  "termsTerminationTitle": "Account Termination",
  "termsTerminationContent": "We have the right to suspend or terminate your account in case of violation of these terms or misuse of the service. You can delete your account at any time through the app settings, knowing that some data may be retained for legal or regulatory purposes. Upon account termination, you will lose access to all features and associated data.",
  "termsChangesTitle": "Changes to Terms",
  "termsChangesContent": "We reserve the right to modify these terms and conditions at any time without prior notice. Users will be notified of any substantial changes via the app or email. Your continued use of the app after modifications means your agreement to the new terms. We advise reviewing this page regularly to stay informed of any updates.",
  "termsContactTitle": "Contact Information",
  "termsContactContent": "If you have any inquiries or comments about these terms and conditions, you can contact us via email: support@qoot.app or through the help section in the app. We are committed to responding to all inquiries within 48 working hours. Qoot support team is always available to help you and solve any problem you may face.",
  "termsLastUpdated": "Last updated: November 2025",
  "faqTitle": "Frequently Asked Questions",
  "faqSubtitle": "Answers to the most common questions about the Qoot platform",
  "faqDonationProcessQuestion": "How does the food donation process work?",
  "faqDonationProcessAnswer": "Restaurants can create a new donation through the 'Create Donation' section, where they enter food details such as type, quantity, expiration date, and contact information. Donations then become available for charities to reserve. The donated food must be safe for consumption and comply with food safety standards.",
  "faqReservationQuestion": "How do charities reserve donations?",
  "faqReservationAnswer": "Charities can browse all available donations through the home page or 'Donations' section. When selecting a specific donation, they can tap 'Reserve Now' to confirm the reservation. The restaurant will be notified immediately, and the charity can track the reservation status through 'My Reservations'. They must adhere to the specified pickup time.",
  "faqFoodSafetyQuestion": "What are the required food safety standards?",
  "faqFoodSafetyAnswer": "Restaurants must ensure that donated food is fresh, stored at safe temperatures, and free from any damage. We recommend reviewing the 'Food Safety Tips' section for best practices in storage and handling. Charities should inspect the food upon receipt and verify its validity before distribution.",
  "faqCancelReservationQuestion": "Can reservations be cancelled?",
  "faqCancelReservationAnswer": "Yes, charities can cancel a reservation by going to 'My Reservations' and selecting the reservation to cancel. We recommend cancelling early if pickup is not possible to allow other charities the opportunity. Restaurants can also cancel a donation in case of an emergency.",
  "faqPickupTimeQuestion": "What is the specified time for picking up donations?",
  "faqPickupTimeAnswer": "The pickup time is set by the restaurant when creating the donation. Charities must adhere to the specified time to ensure food quality and safety. In case of delay, please contact the restaurant directly using the contact information in the donation details.",
  "faqAccountTypesQuestion": "What account types are available?",
  "faqAccountTypesAnswer": "The Qoot platform provides two account types: Restaurant accounts for food donors, and Charity accounts for beneficiaries. Each account has its own interface and features designed to meet its needs. Registration can be done using email or Google and Apple accounts.",
  "faqNotificationsQuestion": "How do I receive notifications?",
  "faqNotificationsAnswer": "Instant notifications are sent when a new donation is created, a reservation is confirmed, or any important update occurs. You can enable notifications from the app settings. Make sure to grant the app notification permission to receive updates in a timely manner.",
  "faqContactSupportQuestion": "How can I contact technical support?",
  "faqContactSupportAnswer": "You can contact us via email: support@qoot.app or through the 'Help' section in the app. The support team is available to respond to your inquiries within 48 working hours. We are committed to providing the best service and helping resolve any issues you may encounter.",
